      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1072,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "##  5. Fetch Slack users and notify them\nThis section pulls all Slack users, filters out bot accounts, and loops through human users one by one. Each user receives a direct message (currently a test text, but later can include task summaries or links) so that the team stays aware of captured tasks."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7f4adc7b-6011-41fc-ba6d-f0a6bbe7e907",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -112,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 736,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "\n# Task Creator Workflow\n## How it works:\nThis workflow watches a Google Drive folder for new task screenshots, downloads them, and uses AI to extract tasks, priorities, and deadlines. Extracted tasks are structured and saved to Google Sheets for tracking. It then notifies relevant Slack users through direct messages with task details, filtering out bots and using API calls to open DM channels before sending notifications, ensuring team members are alerted to new action items from screenshots.\n## Setup Steps:\n1. Trigger and Download Monitor Google Drive folder for new files and download uploaded screenshot using Google Drive Trigger and Download nodes.\n2. Extract and Parse Tasks Analyze image with GPT-4o-mini to identify tasks, then parse JSON response into structured task array using JavaScript.\n3. Structure and Log Data Map tasks with file name, source link, priority, due date, and timestamp, then append to Google Sheets.\n4. Fetch and Filter Users Get Slack workspace users using Slack Get Many Users node and exclude bot accounts using IF condition.\n5. Loop and Open DM Process each valid user through Loop Over Items and call Slack conversations.open API to create direct message channel.\n6. Send and Validate Notification Deliver task details to opened DM channel using Slack Send Message and confirm channel ID mapping from API response.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
